 "headline": "Stereo gets nothing back from the trench floor; the missing-ground detector turns that gap into a lethal ditch band about 5 m ahead",
 "caption": "DEV seed 109 (F2 ditch field). The trench is 1.04 m wide, 0.87 m deep and spans 4.5 to 5.6 m ahead (ground truth). Stereo returns no point more than 0.3 m below the lip inside it (it cannot see the floor), and the missing-ground detector marks the gap as a lethal magenta band at about 4.6 to 5.7 m (central 4 m). Artefacts: a spurious 50-cell ditch streak 2.2 to 3.2 m to the right, out to 7.9 m; 165 amber and 14 red cells farther out; bright horizon mismatches at the top of the disparity map. The trench is 3.5 times as wide as the 0.3 m design ditch, so this frame is not a detection-range result. Hatched: certified ground, where a 0.3 m design ditch would already be visible (to about 4.2 m here; the design ditch resolves to 4.3 m on level ground, Estimated). The speed governor counts only certified ground. Illustrative frame, hand-picked from 20 rendered poses; a single frame from a fresh Perception node (no fusion, no segmenter), software-rendered (SwiftShader). Not a closed-loop result.",
